# Utils, DB layer, config, constants

## src/utils/ — shared helpers
The only place cross-folder logic lives — any function needed by more than one `src/` subfolder.
```python
# Good — takes context/config explicitly, fully typed, logs via context.log
def coalesce_concept(facts: dict, candidates: list[str], context: Context) -> pd.DataFrame:
    context.log.info(f"coalescing {candidates}")
    ...
```
- Pass `context` / `config` explicitly — no global logger or hidden state.
- `context.log` for logging — never `print()`.
- Full type hints on every signature; one logical concern per file.

## src/data_store/ — the DB layer
`DataStore` (`store.py`) is the single tabular I/O path — dialect-aware (Postgres / SQLite):
- `load(table, columns=…)` · `save(table, df)` (upsert on PK) · `replace(table, df)` (truncate + COPY
  full rebuild) · `existing_dates(table, …)` (incremental resume) · `ensure_columns` (auto-ALTER to
  add new DataFrame columns — schema evolution).
- Logical tables are declared in `schema_registry.py` (name → PK + date col); `schema_sql.py`
  regenerates `sql/schema.sql`. Identifier-like numeric codes (`cik`) are TEXT (keep leading zeros).
- Never open raw SQL / parquet from feature code — always go through the store.

## src/constants/constants.py — single source of truth
Every column name, key, URL, date format, env-var key, and threshold used in more than one place is
declared here. Grep first; if it exists, import it; if not, add it before using.

## configs/*.yml — OmegaConf
Loaded via OmegaConf; one yml per stage (`build_cube.yml`, `modellling.yml`, `backtest.yml`,
`peers.yml`, `paths.yml`, `configs.yml`).
- All numeric hyperparameters / windows / thresholds in config — never hardcoded.
- Access via `self._config.<section>.<key>`; defaults always present.

## src/context.py — shared runtime (risk zone)
`Context` is passed through every step and owns:
- `context.config` — the OmegaConf tree
- `context.log` — the logger (never `print()` / `logging.getLogger()` in app code)
- `context.store` — the `DataStore` (all tabular I/O)
- `context.paths` — NON-tabular artifact paths only (models, plots, `sec_bulk_cache/`, filing text)

Infrastructure, not business logic. Changes cascade to every class — treat it as a risk zone.
